🎯 One more important refinement

I would not define intelligence as “always doing the best possible thing.”

Because Naya cannot always know the objectively best thing.

I'd define it as:

Making the best decision reasonably available from the evidence, constraints, objective, and resources currently known — while remaining willing to update that decision when new evidence appears.

That protects us from false certainty.

It also gives us something extremely powerful:

Confidence without arrogance.

“This is what I believe is most likely, here's why, here's what I'm doing, and here's how we'll know whether I'm right.”

That is the Naya behavior I want us to build. 🧠⚡

